            "columns_description" :
              [
                "Lists the name of the location of the furthest registered CPE that the licensee identified as served by this base station ",
                "A unique system assigned identifier for the license.   This identifier is the same license ID used by the legacy ULS systems. ",
                "This field contains the justification provided by the licensee when they have identified equipment as a base station which has been designated for other use (eg CPE) by the FCC",
                "Receipt date of location registration application",
                "Identifies whether the licensee indicated that registered CPEs are deployed.",
                "A sequential number identifying the location ",
                "A site name, provided by the licensee, that describes the location",
                "The upper frequency band edge in MHz",
                "The height above ground level to the highest point of the supporting structure only",
                "The overall height above ground level of the entire antenna structure to the highest point, including any appurtenances",
                "The direction of the lower half-power point of the antenna's main lobe measured in degrees clockwise from true north in the horizontal plane",
                "The direction of the upper half-power point of the antenna's main lobe measured in degrees clockwise from true north in the horizontal plane",
                "The center frequency or lower frequency band edge in MHz",
                "The longitude of the transmitter location in decimal degrees referenced to NAD83",
                "The latitude of the transmitter location in decimal degrees referenced to NAD83",
                "The gain of the transmitting antenna in decibels referenced to an isotropic radiator (dBi)",
                "The FCC identification number of the transmitter",
                "The date the authorization expires",
                "The transmitter emission designator, composed of its necessary bandwidth and emission type",
                "The elevation above mean sea level (AMSL) of the ground at the antenna location",
                "Effective Isotropic Radiated Power in dBm",
                "This field contains the justification provided by the licensee when the distance between the base station and furthest CPE exceeds 18 km",
                "The certifiers role, function or job title",
                "The middle initial of the certifying party",
                "The last name of the certifying party",
                "The date that the user made the required certification when submitting an application",
                "This field contains the justification provided by the licensee when they have identified equipment as a CPE which has been designated for other use (eg Base) by the FCC",
                "The model number of the transmitting antenna",
                "The date of the last update",
                "The direction the transmitter antenna points in degrees toward the farthest registered CPE",
                "The city in which the transmitter is located",
                "The angular distance between the half power points of the antenna’s major lobe in the horizontal plane",
                "The geographic coordinates of the transmit location in DD-MM-SS.S referenced to NAD83",
                "The date the current location status became effective",
                "The FCC assigned designator used to identify a license",
                "A unique system assigned identifier for the location.   This identifier is the same license ID used by the legacy ULS systems. ",
                "The name of the manufacturer of the transmitting antenna",
                "Identifies whether the licensee indicated that un-registered CPEs are deployed.",
                "Identifies whether the licensee has certified that  as of April 17, 2016 this station was Constructed, in Service, and in Compliance with the prior existing rules for 3650-3700 MHz as described in the Commission's 3.5 GHz Order, FCC 15-47 at Paragraph 403",
                "The intended purpose of the equipment i.e. \"base\" \"CPE\" \"dual purpose/point-to-point\" as understood by the FCC",
                "The state in which the transmitter is located",
                "The status of the application i.e. \"submitted\"= under FCC review , \"accepted\"= accepted by the FCC and used to define the grandfathered wireless protection zone, \"rejected\" = rejected by the FCC and not used to define the grandfathered wireless protection zone",
                "The first name of the certifying party",
                "Identifies whether the licensee indicated that the site is being operated as a base station or access point",
                "The FCC assigned file number for an application",
                "The elevation angle of the transmitting antenna measured from the horizontal up to the center line of the main beam of the antenna",
                "The height above ground level to the center of the transmitting antenna in meters above ground level",
                "The FCC Registration Number is a unique identifier given to entities doing business with the Commission",
                "The name of the Licensee of record",
                "Transmission methods or protocols may fall into two categories, unrestricted or restricted",
                "The distance between the base station and the furthest associated CPE",
                "The county in which the transmitter is located",
                "The direction of the main lobe of the transmitter antenna measured in degrees clockwise from True North",
                "The suffix of the certifying party i.e. \"Jr\" \"Sr\" "
              ],
